Initial values:
x = outer-x
y = outer-y

Inside first if block:
x = if-block-x (should be 'if-block-x' - shadowing outer x)
y = outer-y (should be 'outer-y' - using outer y)
z = if-block-z (should be 'if-block-z' - new variable)

Inside nested if block:
x = nested-if-x (should be 'nested-if-x' - shadowing previous x)
y = outer-y (should be 'outer-y' - still using outer y)
z = if-block-z (should be 'if-block-z' - using z from outer block)

After nested if block:
x = if-block-x (should be 'if-block-x' - reverted to first shadow)
z = if-block-z (should be 'if-block-z' - still accessible)

After exiting if block:
x = outer-x (should be 'outer-x' - reverted to original)
y = outer-y (should be 'outer-y' - unchanged)

